# Frontend rules

## Look and feel
- Dark enterprise SOC console. Inspired by modern security platforms, but never copy a product,
  logo, or branding.
- Do NOT use:
  - Matrix effects or neon green
  - Hacker imagery or giant lock icons
  - Gamer UI or heavy glow

## Design tokens
Define tokens once in `tailwind.config.ts` and `src/styles/tokens.css`. Never hardcode hex
values in components.

| Token | Value |
|---|---|
| bg | `#0B0F17` |
| surface | `#111827` |
| surface-2 | `#151C28` |
| border | `#1F2A3A` |
| text | `#E5E7EB` |
| text-muted | `#9CA3AF` |
| accent | `#22D3EE` (cyan) |
| critical | `#EF4444` |
| high | `#F97316` |
| medium | `#F59E0B` |
| low | `#3B82F6` |
| ok | `#22C55E` |

- Use one font family (Inter or system UI) and a fixed type scale.
- Use 4px spacing steps.

## Accessibility
- Severity is never shown by color alone. Always pair it with a text label
  (`<SeverityBadge>`).
- Keyboard focus rings must be visible.
- Charts need readable contrast.

## Architecture
```
frontend/src/
  components/   reusable UI (Card, KpiCard, SeverityBadge, StatusPill, DataTable, PageHeader, DemoBanner)
  pages/        one file per sidebar page
  charts/       Recharts wrappers, themed with tokens
  hooks/        data hooks (useIncidents, useAlerts...)
  services/     api client + data source switch
  fixtures/     DEMO data only, every file starts with a "DEMO DATA" comment
  types/        shared TS types that mirror backend schemas
```

## Data access
- Components never call `fetch` directly. They go through `services/api.ts`.
- `VITE_DATA_MODE=demo|live` controls the data source.
  - In `demo` mode, `<DemoBanner>` is always visible.
- Show loading, empty, and error states on every data panel.
  - An empty state says "No data yet". It never invents numbers.

## Code
- TypeScript strict mode. No `any` without a comment explaining why.
- Keep pages thin. Logic goes in hooks and services.
- Run `npm run lint` and `npm run build`; both must pass before saying a task is done.
